[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Early Bd3"]
[ECO "B12"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-trade"]
[Refutes "1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Bd3"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "4...Bf5"]
[Start "short-system 3...Bf5"]

4. Bd3 $6 { Looks natural, but ...Bxd3 trades off Black's problem piece for White's good one. The right move is 4.Nf3. } 4... Bxd3 { Takes at once. White's good bishop disappears, and Black's own bishop, the piece ...e6 could have shut in, has done its job. } 5. Qxd3 e6 { Black has swapped away the bishop that e5 was cramping, and can now break with ...c5 and ...Nc6 in comfort. } *
